Functions:
return uct done
create node
recursive delete node (not needed in python)

When opponent chooses move,
1. locate child node for resulting state
2. separate it from original tree
3. delete original tree
4. set child node as root
5. build rest of tree

Current state (root)
Possible moves this turn.... (rollouts (1st iter/skipped potentially), UCT (2nd iter), return best UCT (4th iter)) b
Possible opponent moves.... (new root) (rollouts (2nd iter), UCT (3rd iter)) ab
Possible moves for us to choose from next turn.... (rollouts (3rd iter), UCT(4th iter/final)) a^2b
if a = 1, total work is O(b); set exploration parameter(c) to sqrt(2)?

MCTS Tree building:

Selection:
you are on this current node
to check if you've run rollouts on children, check if child list is empty
if child list is not empty, then run UCT because you have wins and traversal counts already

Expansion and Simulation:
if child list is empty, you add all children to frontier (queue) and simulate rollouts (multithreading???)

Backpropagation:
update wins and traversal for children (could be done inside simulation portion)
we update wins and traversal for current node.  now you can do UCT